    {
      "id": 20,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "relay drops/sec",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 10,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 5
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 5,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.001
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(redpanda_relay_dropped_total[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "dropped/s",
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "description": "MUST be zero. The relay is best-effort: a consumer that falls behind has its oldest queued record dropped rather than the producer being slowed down. Any non-zero value here means the latency on this dashboard is the latency of an incomplete stream, and the run is not comparable to one without drops.",
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "text": {
          "titleSize": 14,
          "valueSize": 42
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "active subscriptions",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 6,
        "y": 10,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 5
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 5,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(redpanda_relay_active_subscriptions)",
          "legendFormat": "subscriptions",
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "description": "Subscriptions, NOT consumers. Each consumer transform gets a processor per input partition it leads, so the cluster-wide sum is (consumers x partitions led) - measured at 1,500 for 500 consumers over 3 partitions, which is correct and not a 3x overshoot. What matters is that it is STABLE during a window and that it did not collapse partway through; a figure that moves mid-run means processors were restarting, and the latency spans a changing fan-out.",
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "text": {
          "titleSize": 14,
          "valueSize": 42
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 22,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "relay throughput",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 10,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 5
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 5,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(redpanda_relay_pushes_total[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "pushes/s",
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(redpanda_relay_delivered_total[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "delivered/s",
          "refId": "B",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(redpanda_relay_dropped_total[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "dropped/s",
          "refId": "C",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "description": "delivered/s divided by pushes/s is NOT the fan-out factor, and reading it that way is a mistake this panel used to invite. pushes_total is incremented inside deliver_locally(), which push() calls once for the producer's own shard plus once per other shard holding a subscriber - so it counts shard-delivery passes and grows with how widely subscribers are spread, not with the offered rate. Measured at 500 consumers over 13 shards: 780,000 pushes for 30,000,000 deliveries, a ratio of 38.5, while the actual fan-out was exactly 500. The run's own report computes both and names them apart (relay_delivered_per_shard_pass vs relay_delivered_per_logical_push); the logical figure needs the order count, which Prometheus does not have. What to read here is that delivered tracks pushes smoothly and dropped stays flat at zero.",
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
